== 2. g3 ==
This is a principled move similar to the King's Indian Attack that allows White to [[wikipedia:fianchetto|fianchetto]] a bishop next move. Black's most popular response is [[/2...Nf6/]] followed by 3...g6 3...d6, or 3...e6 to protect the f-pawn but Black could also prepare 3...e5 with [[/2...d6/]] to take the center.

