== 4...b5 ==
This guards c4 and is the best move. The queenside weaknesses are not a problem, as the knight on c3 is vulnerable to b-pawn attacks with ...b4. Note that '''[[/5. Nxb5|5. Nxb5?]]''', trying to exploit the long diagonal to destroy Black's queenside, is a mistake, and gives up the advantage to Black. A common motif in these positions is for Black to play b5 in order to boot the knight, often giving up the c4-pawn in the process.

When your opponent has a space advantage, you want to use pawn breaks to break up their pawn chains. '''[[/5. a4/]]''' is the most effective way to do that. The alternative '''5. b3?!''' Qa5 results in Black being able to put a lot of pressure on White's queenside.

