== 6. O-O ==
White castles their king to safety.

Black's main response is '''[[/6...a6/]]''', looking to develop the light-squared bishop with ...b5 while gaining a tempo on Whites bishop.

'''[[/6...Nc6/]]''' is a sideline, where Black postpones development of their light-squared bishop. The knight may go to a5 in the future to harass Whites bishop.

'''[[/6...cxd4/]]''', the '''Steinitz variation''' results in an isolated queens pawn position. It is still too early to resolve the central tension, since this allows White to develop their pieces fairly comfortably.

