== 4...dxc4 · Vienna variation ==
'''4...dxc4''' is a very aggressive response by Black leading to very double-edged positions. Black gives up some central control, allowing for White to build up a big center that Black tries to tear down later. 

[[/5. e4|'''5. e4''']] is White's main response, taking up the entire center and preparing to recapture the pawn with the bishop. 

[[/5. e3|'''5. e3''']] is the quiet variation. Positions often resemble those of the [[Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5/2. c4/2...dxc4/3. Nf3|Queens Gambit accepted]] with 3. Nf3.

'''[[Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5/2. c4/2...e6/3. Nc3/3...Nf6/4. Nf3/4...dxc4/5. Qa4+|5. Qa4+]]''' is a sideline with positions similar to the [[Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5/2. c4/2...e6/3. Nc3/3...Nf6/4. Nf3/4...c6|Semi Slav defence]].



