== 3...b6 ==
{{chess/sideline}}
Black prepares ...Bb7, to exert long term pressure on the long light square diagonal and further control e4. 

This move order makes it harder for White to play g3 and Bg2, as Black's bishop gets to contest the diagonal first. A continuation is '''4. Nf3''' to prepare g2, and 4...e6 5. g3 Bb7 6. Bg2 Bb4.

=== History ===
The earliest recorded game played in this line was played between Remo Calapso and Ernesto Hellmann at the 1924 Italian national tournament<ref>Remo Calapso vs Erensto Hellmann, Torneo Nazionale A. Folgiono, Italy. September 1924. From [https://federscacchi.it/str_archpart.php the Federsacchi match archive].</ref> (see sample game). 

Another early game was played between Carlos Portela and Alexander Alekhine, 1926.<ref>[https://www.chessgames.com/perl/chessgame?gid=1012430 Portela v Alekhine, 1926. Chessgames.com]</reF>

