== 3. Bg2 ==
White finishes their fianchetto. Black has to reveal their what type of structure they want to play.

'''[[/3...g6/]]''' is the most popular move, entering the '''Leningrad variation'''. The intent of this move is to fianchetto the dark-squared bishop and quickly castle kingside.

'''[[/3...e6/]]''' is the '''Classical variation'''. This opening often has ideas similar to the '''[[Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...Nf6/2. c4/2...e6/3. Nc3/3...Bb4|Nimzo-Indian Defence]]''', although this isn't required, as Black can also go for a Stonewall structure or develop the bishop to e7.

'''[[/3...d5/]]''' is an attempt to enter the '''Stonewall variation'''. Black's main ideas are to reinforce their d-pawn with ...c6 and ...e6, while the pawns on f5 and d5 take control over the e4-square. This plan builds up against White's light-squared bishop, but does leave Black with major dark-squared weaknesses in return, for which their dark-squared bishop has to compensate. It also leaves a hole on e5, where White can try to plant one of their pieces, which then cannot be kicked out by pawns.

'''3...d6''' intends to take control over e5 immediately. This usually transposes into the Leningrad variation, where ...d6 with the intention of ...e5 is one of Black's main ideas.

