== 2. Nc3!? ==
White defends e4 while developing a piece. This is solid but less testing than 2. e5.

This allows Black to play [[/2...e5|'''2...e5''']] and transpose into a Vienna game. 

However, if Black thinks White is too eager to avoid the Alekhine's defence then they may avoid transposing with [[/2...d5|'''2...d5''']], the '''Scandinavian variation'''.

