== 6. g4 · Hibbins-Khan Variation ==
'''6. g4''' is the critical answer to 5...Bf5 and the most ambitious way of handling the Mieses Attack. The pawn hits the undefended bishop and claims space on the kingside.

The bishop usually retreats with '''6...Bg6'''. White then plays h4, intending to chase the bishop again, with Ne2 and Nf4 as a further idea. A typical continuation is 7. h4 h5 8. g5 Nd5 9. e2 e6, with white keeping the initiative on the kingside.<ref>[https://lichess.org/J1qwsG6O Ditrealman v StrapoChi02M, Lichess 2026]</ref>

