== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 3. f4?! ===
An interesting gambit. White gives up their f-pawn, offering a transposition to the Cozio Defence of the King's Gambit if Black accepts the gambit with [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...exf4|3...exf4]]. However, Black can choose to take the e-pawn with [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4|3...Nxe4]] instead, and White cannot play 4. fxe5?? as 4...Qh4+! starts a powerful attack.

{{ChessFooter}}

