== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 3...Nxe4 ===
Black captures the free e-pawn with their knight. White cannot take Black's own e-pawn with [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. fxe5|4. fxe5??]], as after 4...Qh4+! a powerful attack is launched on White's king. White's best move is [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. d3|4. d3]], attacking the knight, and now 4...Qh4+ comes with less attacking power than if 4. fxe5?? were played.

{{ChessFooter}}

{{Chess Opening Theory/Position|=
|Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit
}}
== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 4. d3 ===
White attacks Black's knight and avoids losing material with the tempting 4. fxe5??. Black can choose to retreat it with [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. d3/4...Nd6|4...Nd6]], or try the same attacking idea if White played 4. fxe5??, [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. d3/4...Qh4+|4...Qh4+]]. However, unlike the fxe5 version, 4...Qh4+ does not win a rook as after 5. g3! Nxg3 6. Nf3! the queen cannot go to e4 to check the White king and then take the rook on h1 with the knight on g3.

{{ChessFooter}}

{{Chess Opening Theory/Position|=
|Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit
}}
== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 4. fxe5?? ===
White got way too greedy and captured the seemingly free pawn on e5, but at a cost: [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. fxe5/4...Qh4|4...Qh4+!]] starts an overwhelming attack on White's king which will either win material or checkmate White.

{{ChessFooter}}

{{Chess Opening Theory/Position|=
