== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 4...Qh4+! ===
Black punishes White's careless 4. fxe5?? and will now either win material or checkmate the White king. White has three legal moves: [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. fxe5/4...Qh4/5. Kf1|5. Kf1??]] gets checkmated immediately to 5...Qf2#, [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. fxe5/4...Qh4/5. Ke2|5. Ke2?]] leads to a long forced checkmate sequence after 5...Qf2+ 6. Kd3 Nc5+, and [[Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Bc4/2...Nf6/3. f4/3...Nxe4/4. fxe5/4...Qh4/5. g3|5. g3]] is the only non-losing move, but it will still lose a rook after 5...Nxg3 6. Nf3 Qe4+.

{{ChessFooter}}

{{Chess Opening Theory/Position|=
|Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit
}}
== Bishop's Opening: Berlin Defence, Greco Gambit ==
=== 5. Ke2? ===
White tries to avoid the loss of their rook, but in fact this leads to a long checkmating sequence after 5...Qf2+ 6. Kd3 Nc5+, where Stockfish says that there is a forced mate in 12 after 6...Nc5+.

