== '''3...f5''' ==
This is the Ponziani Countergambit. It sacrifices the f-pawn, but attacks e4 and prepares to develop the knight on g1. While 4.exf5 is a good move, 4.d4 is probably a better option. If White has studied against this, Black will have a bad time, but if not, both sides will be able to attack in an exciting game.

