== 4. Nd3?! · Karklins-Martinovsky variation ==
'''4. Nd3?!''' retreats the knight to d3, keeping the piece safe while avoiding the more common retreats to f3 or c4.

The main drawback of this move is that the knight on d3 blocks the d-pawn and may interfere with White's central pawn development. 

