== 4...d5 · Polerio-Svedenborg variation ==

The best and most common move. Black now is attacking White's bishop on c4 and preventing Nf7. But 4. Nxe5 carried a second threat: '''[[/5. Qh5|5. Qh5+!]]'''. However, if Black finds 5...g6!? to sacrifice the exchange after 6. Nxg6 hxg6 7. Qxh8 Kf7!, the position is objectively equal.

It's true that White can save the bishop with 5. Bb5+ or 5. Be2 (5. Bb3?? loses to 5...Qg5!), but it lacks the aggression and force of Qh5+, so 5. Qh5+ is more preferred.

