== 5...Bd7 · Euwe variation ==
With '''5...Bd7''', Black enters the '''Euwe Variation'''.<ref>[http://www.365chess.com/opening.php?m=11&n=1250&ms=e4.e6.d4.d5.e5.c5.c3.Nc6.Nf3.Bd7&ns=3.16.12.17.453.525.454.526.711.1250]</ref> This move is less committal than the main line [[../5...Qb6|5...Qb6]], as it allows Black to reserve the option of where to place their Queen. In some lines, Black may prefer an eventual ...Qc7, adding pressure to e5. This move also prepares Black's thematically weak light-square Bishop for a possible escape to b5 or a4.

After both of White's most popular options, '''6. Be2''' and '''6. a3''', Black has many different ways to develop their pieces. A common idea in both lines is the thematic 6...f6, after which Black usually takes on e5 and plays ...Qc7 followed by ...O-O-O, with a very double-edged game to follow. 6...Nge7 followed by Ng6 or Nf5 is another manoeuvre thematic to the French that occurs often in these positions. 

